---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Terms of Use — apprenti.dev">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Terms of Use</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">Last updated: August 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    1. Acceptance of terms
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    These Terms of Use ("<strong class="text-foreground"
                        >Terms</strong
                    >") govern your use of
                    <a href="/" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >apprenti.dev</a
                    > and the associated application (collectively, the "<strong
                        class="text-foreground">App</strong
                    >"). By installing, accessing, or using the App, you agree
                    to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
                    For how the App handles data, see our
                    <a href="/docs/privacy" class="text-link hover:underline"
                        >Privacy Policy</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    2. What apprenti.dev is
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    apprenti.dev is a free, Git-native, offline-first
                    apprenticeship app. It runs on Android, iOS, Windows,
                    macOS, and Linux. There is no user account and no
                    application backend: your curriculum, progress,
                    reflections, and submissions are stored as files in a Git
                    repository that you host, on a provider you choose (such
                    as GitHub or GitLab). Optional AI features can run fully
                    on-device or, if you configure one, through a third-party
                    cloud AI provider using an API key you supply yourself.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    3. License and use grant
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    apprenti.dev is provided to you free of charge. You are
                    granted a limited, non-exclusive, revocable right to
                    install and use the App for personal or organizational
                    apprenticeship, mentoring, and curriculum-authoring
                    purposes. These Terms do not grant you any rights in the
                    App's underlying source code beyond what is separately
                    published and licensed in its public repository, if any;
                    absent a separate license grant stated there, no rights
                    to copy, redistribute, or create derivative works of the
                    App's code are given by these Terms.
                </p>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Because apprenti.dev is Git-native, curriculum content is
                    designed to be forkable: you may fork, adapt, and share a
                    curriculum repository through ordinary Git operations,
                    subject to whatever license or terms the specific
                    curriculum's author has attached to it. Forking a
                    curriculum does not transfer any rights to the App
                    itself.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    4. Your content
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Your curriculum data, task state, notes, reflections,
                    evidence, submissions, and mentor reviews live in Git
                    repositories that you control and host yourself.
                    apprenti.dev does not host this content, does not have a
                    copy of it, and claims no ownership over it. You are
                    solely responsible for your content, for who you share
                    repository access with, and for complying with the terms
                    of whatever Git host and, where applicable, whatever
                    curriculum license governs it.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    5. AI features
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    AI features are optional and assistive — they do not
                    replace mentor judgment and never auto-approve a
                    submission or otherwise change review state on their own.
                    You may run AI features fully offline using a local
                    model, or connect a third-party cloud AI provider (for
                    example OpenAI, Mistral, Anthropic, or OpenRouter) using
                    your own API key. If you choose a cloud provider, your
                    use of that provider is governed by that provider's own
                    terms of service and privacy policy, not these Terms.
                    apprenti.dev is not responsible for the availability,
                    output, or accuracy of any third-party AI provider.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
